Ani, Farida,

Thank you for running it last night, and thank you for the ACTIVE_FLG point
below. That was not on my list and it should have been.

Where this sits as of this morning.

The rule is DQ-R-15. Dimension is validity. The statement is that the GST rate
carried on a fact row matches the rate that was in force on the invoice date.
Threshold 99.9%.

At the 31-May-2026 profiling run the actual was 96.3%, which is a fail, and
that is what VAR-006 was opened against. I re-ran the same rule against the new
structure at about eight this morning and it is back inside the threshold. I am
deliberately not putting a new percentage into the pack. Every profiling figure
in the assessment is stated as of the 31-May run across the fourteen tables and
I am not going to have two run dates sitting in one document. The next full
profiling run restates all of them together or none of them.

The defect itself, written down in one place so that we stop explaining it on
calls:

1. BCPL_EDW.TAX_RATE_MASTER was a straight truncate and reload copy of
   FIN_PROD.TAX_RATE_MASTER, holding current rates only. No EFF_START_DT, no
   EFF_END_DT, no CURRENT_FLG. 214 rows at the 31-May run.
2. The source table is effective dated. The warehouse copy was not. That
   asymmetry is the whole of the defect, there is nothing cleverer going on.
3. Consequence. Chandanaa, HSN 3401, moved from 18 percent to 12 percent with
   effect from 01-Oct-2025. Because the warehouse only ever held the current
   rate, invoice lines from April to September 2025 were resolving 12 percent
   as well, retrospectively. The rate that was actually applied on the invoice
   is correct in ORION. The picture in the warehouse was wrong.
4. The register carries 40 L against it, INR 39,60,000, FY26. I have not
   re-derived that and I am not proposing to.
5. Remediated by DIM_TAX_RATE, effective dated, under CHG0021339, deployed
   26.08.2026.

Two asks and one hold.

Ani, on ACTIVE_FLG and DELETE_FLAG on the source table. Can you or Karthik
confirm what the new mapping is actually picking up. If it is taking every
source row regardless of those two flags then DQ-R-15 will pass and the
dimension will still be carrying rows that were never live, and a rule that
passes for the wrong reason is worse than one that fails honestly.

Meghna, when the profiling job is free, can you re-run the HSN 3401 comparison
on a sample and send me the counts with the run date on them. Not urgent. I
want it in the evidence folder before the pack goes out, not after somebody
asks for it.

Shalini, subject to the above I will move VAR-006 to closed tomorrow. If you
want the restated tax lines tied back to the trial balance before I do that,
tell me today and I will hold it. It is your call and not mine.

Regards,
Neha

